// Paste into: Power Apps Studio -> Tree view -> App -> OnStart property
//
// Kept deliberately small. OnStart runs before the first screen paints, so anything
// slow here is felt as launch latency on every single open. Per-screen data loads live
// in each screen's OnVisible.

Set(gblUser, User());

// The board renders one column per Stage choice, read live from SharePoint. Adding a
// stage in the list settings adds a board column with no change to the app.
ClearCollect(colStages, Choices('pursuit-tracker-Pursuits'.Stage));

// Which portfolio the board and list are showing. The mockups say "SI pursuit
// management"; this exists so a second portfolio doesn't require a second app.
Set(gblPortfolio, "SI pursuit management");

// Card currently "picked up" for a stage move. Blank when nothing is selected.
// See docs/07-gaps-and-decisions.md for why this exists instead of drag-and-drop.
Set(gblMoving, Blank());


// =====================================================================
// LoadPortfolio -- the shared refresh used by both the board and the list.
//
// Power Fx has no user-defined behaviour functions in a canvas app, so this block is
// duplicated verbatim into scrPortfolioBoard.OnVisible and scrPortfolioList.OnVisible,
// and re-run after any Patch that changes a stage. Change it here, then paste it into
// both. (A named formula can't do it -- ClearCollect is a side effect.)
// =====================================================================

// Open tasks only. Pulled once and joined in memory rather than looked up per card:
// a per-row LookUp inside a gallery template fires one request per visible card and
// makes the board visibly stutter.
ClearCollect(
    colOpenTasks,
    Filter(
        'pursuit-tracker-Tasks',
        Status.Value <> "Complete"
    )
);

ClearCollect(
    colPortfolio,
    AddColumns(
        Filter(
            'pursuit-tracker-Pursuits',
            IsActive = true,
            Portfolio.Value = gblPortfolio
        ) As P,
        // The whole next-task record, so cards can read .Title, .DueDate and
        // .DueDescription without three separate lookups.
        "NextTask",
        First(
            Sort(
                Filter(colOpenTasks, PursuitKey = P.ID, Not(IsBlank(DueDate))),
                DueDate,
                SortOrder.Ascending
            )
        ),
        // Flattened multi-choice values. Galleries can bind to the raw table, but the
        // Excel export needs them as text and computing it twice invites drift.
        "SIsText",  Concat(P.AlignedSIs, Value, ", "),
        "HypeText", Concat(P.Hyperscalers, Value, ", ")
    )
);
